<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Angola</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Angola is a country in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> that was a Portuguese colony from the late sixteenth century until 1975. It was a major source of enslaved Africans for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a>, especially to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>. Portuguese expansion from Angola affected the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lunda-empire">Lunda Empire</a>'s trade, and the colonial war that began in 1961 contributed to the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/angola.jpg" alt="Angola" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Henrique de Carvalho Santos Vector: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Angola.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
